        "original_id": "28d2821c-1c32-5159-9646-d583e86e8162",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: John Frankenheimer, Tiffanie DeBartolo, Jennifer Aniston, Burt Lancaster, Edward Anhalt, Evan Hunter\n- Works: Dream for an Insomniac, The Young Savages\n- Roles: film director, television director, writer\n- Topics: American film, crime drama films, social dramas, action and suspense films\n\nFacts:\n- John Frankenheimer was born on February 19, 1930, and he became an American film and television director known for social dramas and action and suspense films.\n- The Young Savages is a 1961 crime drama film directed by John Frankenheimer, starring Burt Lancaster, and written by Edward Anhalt from a novel by Evan Hunter.\n- Tiffanie DeBartolo wrote and directed the film Dream for an Insomniac, which featured Jennifer Aniston and had a very limited release in 1996.\n- John Frankenheimer died on July 6, 2002.",
